 "intro": "The imperfect describes how things were, what you always did, and the background of a story.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "era",
   "significado": "I/he/she/you formal was",
   "pron": "E-ra",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is used to describe the past: «era niño», «era alta». It is the same for yo and él: «era».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tenía",
   "significado": "I/he/she/you formal had, used to have",
   "pron": "te-NI-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Verbs in -er and -ir form the imperfect with -ía. The accent marks the í: te-NÍ-a.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "vivía",
   "significado": "I/he/she/you formal lived, used to live",
   "pron": "bi-BI-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is written with v and sounds «b». It is the same for yo and él: «vivía».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "iba",
   "significado": "I/he/she/you formal went, used to go",
   "pron": "I-ba",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Ir» is irregular in the imperfect, but very easy: iba, ibas, iba, íbamos, ibais, iban.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "íbamos",
   "significado": "we went, we used to go",
   "pron": "I-ba-mos",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is the only form of «ir» with an accent in the imperfect: the stressed syllable is the first, Í-ba-mos.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "veía",
   "significado": "I/he/she/you formal saw, used to see",
   "pron": "be-I-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Ver» keeps the e in the imperfect: veía, veías. The accent breaks the diphthong: be-Í-a.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cuando",
   "significado": "when",
   "pron": "KWAN-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "conjunction",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Without an accent, it joins two ideas: «cuando era niño…». With an accent it is a question: «¿cuándo?».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "niño",
   "significado": "child, boy",
   "pron": "NI-nyo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The ñ sounds «ny»: NI-nyo. It is a masculine noun; the feminine is «niña».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "niña",
   "significado": "girl, child (feminine)",
   "pron": "NI-nya",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Change -o to -a: niño, niña. With «cuando era niña» a woman talks about her childhood.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "antes",
   "significado": "before, back then",
   "pron": "AN-tes",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With the imperfect it marks a past habit: «antes vivía aquí». The opposite is «ahora».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "siempre",
   "significado": "always",
   "pron": "SYEM-pre",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It asks for the imperfect when talking about a habit: «siempre iba al parque». It is written with -ie-.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tenías",
   "significado": "you had (tener)",
   "pron": "te-NI-as",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Imperfect: «tenía», «tenías». The accent marks the í.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "ibas",
   "significado": "you went (ir)",
   "pron": "I-bas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Ir» is irregular in the past: «iba», «ibas».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "veías",
   "significado": "you saw (ver)",
   "pron": "be-I-as",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Ver» in the imperfect keeps the e: «veía», «veías».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "jugaba",
   "significado": "I played (jugar)",
   "pron": "hu-GA-ba",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The j sounds like h: «jugaba» is hu-GA-ba.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "andando",
   "significado": "walking (andar)",
   "pron": "an-DAN-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
